One of the questions I get most often from potential clients is: "Do I need all of these services, or can I just do one?"

The honest answer: you can start with one. But the services work better together than any of them do in isolation.

Here's how the pieces connect.

## Strategy Is the Foundation

Everything starts with strategy. Not because it's on the list, but because without it, every other service is less effective.

Strategy answers three questions:
1. Who exactly are we trying to reach?
2. What do we say to them that's different from what our competitors say?
3. Where do we put our marketing energy to get the best return?

Without clear answers to these questions, your SEO optimises for the wrong keywords, your ads target the wrong audiences, and your website converts the wrong visitors.

## Positioning Amplifies Everything

Positioning is the articulation of your strategic answer to "why us?"

A strong positioning statement makes SEO more effective (because you know what search terms matter), makes ads cheaper (because your message resonates with the right audience and gets clicked), and makes the website more effective (because visitors immediately understand what you do and who you do it for).

Weak positioning — "we deliver excellent results" or "we're a full-service agency" — makes every downstream marketing activity harder and more expensive.

## SEO Builds Long-Term Visibility

Once strategy and positioning are clear, SEO has a clear direction. We're not just chasing traffic — we're attracting the specific buyers who match the positioning.

Technical SEO ensures the site can be found. Content strategy builds authority on the topics that matter to the ideal customer. Local SEO captures the Aberdeen and Scotland search opportunity.

SEO compounds over time. The work done in month 3 still generates leads in month 24.

## Paid Media Fills the Gap

SEO is slow. Paid media is fast.

While SEO builds long-term organic traffic, Google Search and LinkedIn ads can generate qualified leads within weeks of launch. The targeting parameters are guided by the strategy: we know who we're trying to reach, so we can target precisely.

The most efficient campaigns use SEO and paid media together: organic content builds trust and retargeting audiences, paid campaigns capture the high-intent buyers.

## Web & CRO Converts the Traffic

All of the above generates visits. The website converts them (or doesn't).

A site that loads slowly, communicates vaguely, or buries the CTA loses leads that all the other work generated. CRO (conversion rate optimisation) ensures the traffic pipeline is as leak-free as possible.

## The Integrated Result

When all these services work together — strategy informing positioning, positioning informing SEO, SEO and paid working together, CRO converting the traffic — the result is a marketing system that compounds.

You don't need all of it at once. Start with the piece that fixes your biggest current problem. Build from there.

If you're not sure where to start, book the free 30-minute strategy review. I'll tell you exactly which piece to prioritise first.
